<title>INDIA: Indian sugar rises on seasonal demand.</title>
<headline>Indian sugar rises on seasonal demand.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sugar prices bounced back on Tuesday on demand from bulk consumers ahead of wedding season, dealers said.</p>
<p>In the ready delivery sugar S-30 rose 10 rupees to 1,215/1,245 per quintal while M-30 climbed 5.0 rupees to 1,240/1,315.</p>
<p>Meanwhile sugar mill delivery was steady at 1,140/1,150 rupees per quintal amid limited enquiries from the outstation buyers, the dealers said.</p>
<p>--Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
